                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game lets you watch a bullet travel 300 meters just to give someone's skeleton a very bad day.\n\nSet in WWII Berlin, Sniper Elite V2 Remastered delivers satisfying long-range shooting, excellent bullet physics, and X-ray kill cams that somehow never get old.\n\nThe downside? Stealth can be clumsy, enemy AI is inconsistent, and some missions force you into firefights when all you wanted was to quietly ruin someone's afternoon.\n\nHas it aged well? Mostly where it matters. The sniping is still great, but the stiff movement, dated AI, and linear mission design definitely show their age. The original visuals are understandably dated, too.\n\nRatings:\n\nGameplay: 8/10\n\nStory: 6/10\n\nGraphics: 7/10 (for 2012)\n\nEnjoyment: 8/10\n\nOverall: 7.5/10 | Recommended\n\nA little rough around the edges, but the sniping still hits. Literally.",
